CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION manager_name(p_department_id IN NUMBER) RETURN VARCHAR2 IS
  l_name employees.last_name%TYPE;
BEGIN
  SELECT e.last_name INTO l_name
    FROM departments d JOIN employees e ON e.employee_id = d.manager_id
   WHERE d.department_id = p_department_id;
  RETURN l_name;
EXCEPTION
  WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN
    RETURN NULL;
END manager_name;
```

This changes only the exception handling. It returns `NULL` when the query finds no row, including when the department has no manager, when `p_department_id` is `NULL`, or when the department id does not exist. If those cases need to be distinguished, that is a business decision and would require additional code.

